00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:04.880
Lisa!

00:22:05.880 --> 00:22:09.830
Mr. Kimball, could you talk to Mr. Douglas and see if he won't take it easy?

00:22:10.290 --> 00:22:13.000
Sure, don't worry. I know how to handle these kind of cases.

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.620
Oh, don't tell him I talk to you.

00:22:15.740 --> 00:22:17.080
Yeah, they just need a little humoring.

00:22:19.420 --> 00:22:21.170
Oh, hello, Mr. Douglas. How are you?

00:22:21.550 --> 00:22:23.830
Oh, I'm all right.

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:27.830
Of course you are. Say, there certainly is a nice-looking horse you got there.

00:22:29.650 --> 00:22:30.000
Oh.

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:32.410
Feed him a piece of sugar.

00:22:34.300 --> 00:22:36.300
Say, look at him eat that.

00:22:36.300 --> 00:22:38.300
Your zebra would like a piece, too.

00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:40.760
Have you been talking to my wife?

00:22:40.760 --> 00:22:42.030
About what?

00:22:42.030 --> 00:22:45.490
About my seeing a horse, a zebra, and a camel.

00:22:45.490 --> 00:22:46.490
A camel?

00:22:46.490 --> 00:22:48.490
She didn't say anything about a...

00:22:48.490 --> 00:22:50.490
Oh, I didn't notice him.

00:22:50.490 --> 00:22:52.490
Say, he certainly isn't...

00:22:52.490 --> 00:22:54.490
Oh, boy.

00:22:54.490 --> 00:22:56.370
I know it's none of my business, Mr. Douglas, but...

00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:57.320
Maybe you've been...

00:22:57.320 --> 00:23:00.000
Is that your chimp over there?

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.300
Would you like a punch in the nose?

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:03.820
No, I don't think I'd like that.

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:05.280
Then stop making fun of me.

00:23:05.720 --> 00:23:07.100
There's a chimp standing there.

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:12.750
That's strange.

00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:14.940
There was a...

00:23:14.940 --> 00:23:15.380
Here, chimp!

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:15.960
Here, chimp!

00:23:15.980 --> 00:23:16.780
Oh, stop!

00:23:18.030 --> 00:23:18.990
Mr. Douglas!

00:23:20.450 --> 00:23:23.690
Mr. Douglas.

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:24.210
What's the matter?

00:23:24.310 --> 00:23:25.570
Did you see a camel?

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:27.760
You too, huh?

00:23:27.920 --> 00:23:30.000
I caught the zebra and the chimp.

00:23:31.950 --> 00:23:33.710
Hey, that's my zebra!

00:23:33.710 --> 00:23:36.250
That's my chimp.

00:23:36.250 --> 00:23:37.360
That's not my chimp.

00:23:37.360 --> 00:23:38.710
Whose chimp is he?

00:23:38.710 --> 00:23:41.410
Well, he belongs to an itinerant circus.

00:23:41.410 --> 00:23:44.590
Their truck turned over and some of the animals got loose.

00:23:44.590 --> 00:23:45.850
Was there a horse?

00:23:45.850 --> 00:23:47.930
Uh, yeah, the fella got him.

00:23:47.930 --> 00:23:50.130
Lisa!

00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:51.800
Darling, what's the matter?

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:53.350
What do you see?

00:23:53.350 --> 00:23:54.510
Mr. Haney's truck.

00:23:54.510 --> 00:23:57.150
No, no, what do you see on the truck?

00:23:57.150 --> 00:23:59.360
What do you want me to see?

00:23:59.360 --> 00:24:00.000
The zebra!

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.380
and a chimpanzee.

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:02.760
I see a zebra

00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:03.600
and a chimpanzee

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:04.440
and I'll call the doctor.

00:24:04.480 --> 00:24:04.780
No, no.

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:06.780
If you don't see them,

00:24:06.820 --> 00:24:07.840
you better call the doctor.

00:24:08.610 --> 00:24:09.690
Well, I see them,

00:24:09.750 --> 00:24:10.530
but I'm not sure

00:24:10.530 --> 00:24:11.550
if they're really there.

00:24:11.850 --> 00:24:12.990
They're there, all right.

00:24:13.110 --> 00:24:14.450
They got loose from the circus.

00:24:15.280 --> 00:24:16.040
Oh, darling,

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:17.000
I'm so glad

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:18.120
you're not a nut.

00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:21.690
Sometimes I wonder.

00:24:23.690 --> 00:24:23.970
Oh,

00:24:31.180 --> 00:24:35.640
Are you missing a boxing kangaroo?
